{"diagnosis": "Loopback RX latched recv_buf_data as 0xe0 instead of expected 0xa5, causing tohost FAIL 0xdead. Start half-bit in state 1 uses full cfg_divider (2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) but data/stop states 10/default sample when recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider>>4), i.e. 1/16th of the bit period. This 16x-early sampling mis-aligns bits and corrupts the byte. Root cause is the >>4 divisor in the excerpt.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,14 +89,14 @@
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end
", "expected": "tohost PASS with uart loopback 0xa5 received correctly, no data mismatch TRAP"}

